        "created_at": 1794532286.1777122
      },
      "rev_n_7_13ea4d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_13ea4d_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_13ea4d",
        "thought_text": "Review the current approach of using inversions to determine bad permutations. The error is in the calculation of total_bad_permutations, which should be the factorial of the sum of inversions, not their product.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5294058945963812840",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532329.6684048
      },
      "rev_n_8_28f490_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_28f490_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_28f490",
        "thought_text": "Consider alternative methods to count good permutations. One approach could be to use dynamic programming to build up the count of good permutations based on the properties of the sequence.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5294058945963812840",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532329.6684234
      },
      "rev_n_9_a9d105_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_a9d105_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_a9d105",
        "thought_text": "Explore the use of combinatorial mathematics to directly calculate the number of good permutations without explicitly counting bad ones. This could involve considering the constraints on the sequence elements and their relative order.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5294058945963812840",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794532329.6684325
      },
      "rev_n_7_13ea4d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_13ea4d_1",
        "node_id": "n_7_13ea4d",
        "thought_text": "The error in the calculation of good permutations was due to incorrectly using the product of inversions instead of their sum. The correct approach is to calculate the total number of bad permutations as the factorial of the sum of inversions in both sequences, and then subtract this from the total number of permutations to get the count of good permutations.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5294058945963812840",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_7_13ea4d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_3546bf9128",
        "created_at": 1794532368.6370616
      },
      "rev_n_6_3da8a0_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_3da8a0_1",
        "node_id": "n_6_3da8a0",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of using the inclusion-exclusion principle is flawed. It incorrectly counts permutations that are bad, leading to an overestimation of good permutations. Instead, we should use dynamic programming to count the number of good sequences directly, considering the constraints on the first and second elements separately.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6227702377633332811",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_6_3da8a0_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_923b81f4c3",
